From 51bd5adfe92aa3010d0b0ddbc417d2be636a369e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DatCaptainHorse <DatCaptainHorse@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 22:00:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] radv: don't make the GE rings BO discardable

amdgpu only adds GTT to a VRAM BO's allowed domains when the BO is not
discardable. A discardable BO that gets evicted loses its backing and
can only be placed in VRAM again, so under VRAM pressure it may never
come back: every submission that references it fails validation with
-ENOMEM ("Not enough memory for command submission") until enough VRAM
is freed, which on a full card can be never.

Seen with several processes sharing an RX 9060 XT under dmem cgroup
protection: a protected allocation in one process evicted another
process's GE rings, and that process then failed every graphics
submission (1735 failed validations in 6 seconds, all of this 4 MiB
BO) while the card stayed full.

Without the flag the BO keeps VRAM as its preferred domain with GTT as
a fallback: under pressure the ring is moved to GTT and the submission
goes through, and it is moved back to VRAM once there is room. The
cost is copying the ring's contents on eviction, which is rare.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/amd/vulkan/radv_queue.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_queue.c b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_queue.c
index e3321ff9b85..ec7a934c78f 100644
--- a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_queue.c
+++ b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_queue.c
@@ -947,8 +947,12 @@ radv_update_preamble_cs(struct radv_queue_state *queue, struct radv_device *devi
 
    if (!queue->ring_info.ge_rings && needs->ge_rings) {
       assert(pdev->info.gfx_level >= GFX11);
+      /* Not discardable: amdgpu gives a discardable BO no GTT fallback, so
+       * once evicted under VRAM pressure it can only come back to VRAM, and
+       * every submission that needs it fails until VRAM frees up.
+       */
       result = radv_bo_create(device, NULL, pdev->info.total_attribute_pos_prim_ring_size, 2 * 1024 * 1024 /* 2MiB */,
-                              RADEON_DOMAIN_VRAM, RADEON_FLAG_32BIT | RADEON_FLAG_DISCARDABLE | ring_bo_flags_tmz,
+                              RADEON_DOMAIN_VRAM, RADEON_FLAG_32BIT | ring_bo_flags_tmz,
                               RADV_BO_PRIORITY_SCRATCH, 0, true, &ge_rings_bo);
       if (result != VK_SUCCESS)
          goto fail;
